  "question": "Does the review Intent's eval job, run from main, read the private held-out home with its environment's secret and upload its eval-report/1 by hashes alone, and is that environment refused to every other branch?",
  "pass": "The job reads and uploads on main, and the environment admits main alone with no admin bypass (section 6). As the story, #309, states it, under the Factory Builder's ruling of 2026-11-09, pre-approved by the Maintainer on 2026-11-08: run 42347416962 of .github/workflows/eval.yml, dispatched on main at its head, concluded success; its fetch step, the one step that reads the home with factory-eval's secret, succeeded, and so did its upload; its artifact eval-report is listed unexpired, and its archive's sha256 is the digest GitHub lists for it; the report names that run's commit, and its set's sha256, count and every case's id and sha256 are those evals/pr-review/cases.json holds at that commit. The environment factory-eval has one deployment branch policy, main, with protected_branches false and can_admins_bypass false, read live: that read stands in for the refusal of a dispatch from another branch. Residual, stated: no dispatch from another branch was exercised. The fixture holds hashes, codes and run metadata alone: no case's content, no case's verdict or reasons, and no secret, nor the list of the environment's secrets, which was not read.",
