            "tree_id": "fe2a466d35ef359b8cf55e1ea322d01e982ddcf2",
            "message": "The artifact storage is any productionresults account numbered in one to three digits (record 0151) (#598)\n\n* The artifact storage is any productionresults account numbered in one to three digits (record NNNN)\n\nThe cut of factory/v0.1.0 was refused with eval_gate_closed: the eval\nreport's download redirected to productionresultssa32, which the\ntransport's STORAGE pattern, sa0 to sa19 by decision 0045, refused, so\nthe report was read as unanswered. By the Maintainer's ruling, the\nstorage is productionresultssa and one to three digits, with no leading\nzero; the rest of 0045's row stands.\n\n- STORAGE in adapters/github.py widened, and a boundary test: sa0 to\n  sa999 accepted; sa1000, a leading zero, a letter or non-ASCII digit\n  in the number, another account name and another host refused.\n- Mutants: a fourth digit, a stop at sa99 or sa19, a leading zero, a\n  trailing letter, Unicode digits, and any account name.\n- Record NNNN replaces 0147, the one record in force of those that hold\n  0045's rows (0045, then 0138, then 0147), and overturns only the\n  accounts 0045's row names. 0147's Status says it is replaced.\n\nEvery artifact read through the redirect, a Run's outcome, a Lens's\napplied/1, the pass records and the eval report, had the same latent\nfailure whenever GitHub served it past sa19.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix round 1 on record 0151: no mutant that no test can kill, and the record named\n\n- The mutant giving the storage's number any Unicode digit is dropped:\n  storage() refuses a URL that is not ASCII before STORAGE is read, so\n  no test can tell it from the code. The record's row no longer claims\n  it (the security pass, the Claude review, Astra and Argon).\n- The record says that every account from sa0 to sa999 being GitHub's\n  is assumed, not known, and what the ruling accepts in it (the\n  security pass).\n- The record says a leading zero is refused, narrower than the ruling,\n  since GitHub's names have none (the Factory Builder).\n- NNNN is 0151, the Factory Builder's number, everywhere (Argon).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
